+    // Flat shading compatibility (port DK64-Recomp Android).
+    //
+    // The proprietary Qualcomm drivers of the Adreno 6xx family (Vulkan 1.1, LA.UM.9.x
+    // builds) fail to link graphics pipelines whose pixel shader declares a flat shaded
+    // varying: the driver logs "Failed to link shaders." and vkCreateGraphicsPipelines
+    // returns VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN. All eight raster uber shader pipelines hit exactly that
+    // path on such drivers (upstream RT64 issue #183 documents the same failure on the
+    // Adreno 618), and the resulting undefined driver state ends up crashing the process
+    // inside vkUpdateDescriptorSets.
+    //
+    // The Flat decoration is a fragment-stage interpolation hint only, so removing it
+    // from the SPIR-V degrades true flat shading into smooth interpolation while keeping
+    // the pipeline perfectly valid. On N64 content the flat color is in most cases
+    // uniform across the primitive, which makes the change visually indistinguishable.
+    // Upstream RT64 plans to replace the flat attribute with vertex duplication for the
+    // same reason (issue #183), which confirms the direction.
+    //
+    // When the driver is detected as unreliable (see RasterShader::detectFlatShadingSupport)
+    // the decorations are stripped from the uber blobs and from every specialized shader
+    // right before they're handed to the driver, so no pipeline creation ever fails.
+
+    static bool g_FlatShadingSupported = true;
+    static bool g_FlatShadingSupportDetected = false;
+
+    // Port DK64-Recomp Android: dual source blending compatibility. The proprietary
+    // Qualcomm drivers of the Adreno 6xx family fail the creation of any graphics
+    // pipeline whose blend state references the secondary source (SRC1_ALPHA /
+    // INV_SRC1_ALPHA): the driver logs "Failed to link shaders." and
+    // vkCreateGraphicsPipelines returns VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN, even though the very same
+    // shader pair links fine when the blend state doesn't reference SRC1. Every
+    // alpha blended raster shader of the smooth shaded family hits exactly that
+    // path on such drivers, which left the game with no visible geometry after the
+    // boot logo. When the driver reports the capability as unreliable (see
+    // RasterShader::detectFlatShadingSupport), the pixel shaders built from the
+    // RASTER_PS_NO_DUAL_SOURCE permutations fold the blend factor into output 0's
+    // alpha channel and the pipelines use standard SRC_ALPHA blending instead.
+    static bool g_DualSourceBlendSupported = true;
+
+    // Removes every "OpDecorate ... Flat" instruction from a SPIR-V module.
